      "modify_from": "For every A, point at the current visible center of the same cube identified by target_anchor, allowing small shifts after placement; use the release trajectory in the current interval to disambiguate nearby cubes. Do not point at the raised wrist or an airborne cube centroid as a table grasp location.",
      "modify_to": "For every A, point at the current visible center of the table cube identified by target_anchor, allowing small placement and visible-center shifts. After a completed release, first select the visible table cube matching the anchor. A clear near-anchor table match takes precedence over inconsistent held-object or airborne-centroid reports during the interval. Use the actual table-height release location and coherent local motion to resolve identity only when the final table view is occluded or genuinely ambiguous. A displaced lifted-cube report alone must not transfer target identity to a different table cube. Do not point at the raised wrist or an airborne cube centroid as a table grasp location."
